  #line-at(54.024pt, 136.46pt, "ABSTRACT ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 148.46pt, "In this work, we demonstrate the first two-port radial-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 159.98pt, "mode Rosen transformer based on 36°Y-cut lithium nio-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 171.5pt, "bate (LN) for piezoelectric power conversion. The device ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 182.9pt, "achieves a high transformation ratio (TF) of 16, a high elec-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 194.42pt, "tromechanical coupling factor (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.37pt, 194.42pt, "k")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.81pt, 190.94pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(189.05pt, 194.42pt, ") of 16.8% and a quality ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 205.94pt, "factor (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(83.424pt, 205.94pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.624pt, 205.94pt, ") of 2500, yielding an outstanding figure of merit ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 217.46pt, "(FoM = ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(87.504pt, 217.46pt, "Q ∙ k")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.7pt, 213.98pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(109.94pt, 217.46pt, ") of 420. The fabricated transformer features ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 228.98pt, "a large effective turns ratio of 16 and delivers an open-cir-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 240.5pt, "cuit voltage gain of 45.56 (unloaded) and 40.57 with a load ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 251.93pt, "of 1 MΩ in parallel with 0.1 pF, validating its ability to ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 263.45pt, "provide efficient passive voltage amplification. An equiva-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 274.97pt, "lent circuit model was developed to accurately fit both fi-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 286.49pt, "nite element-simulated and measured admittance spectra, ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 298.01pt, "enabling reliable parameter extraction. These results estab-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 309.41pt, "lish LN radial-mode resonators as a promising high-perfor-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 320.93pt, "mance, magnetic-less transformer platform. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.024pt, 345.77pt, "KEYWORDS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 357.77pt, "Piezoelectric Transformer, Lithium Niobate, RF-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 369.29pt, "MEMS, Voltage Amplifier ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.024pt, 394.13pt, "INTRODUCTION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 406.01pt, "As power systems strive for higher power density, ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 417.55pt, "magnetic transformers face increasing core losses, parasitic ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 429.07pt, "effects, and material constraints that limit further miniatur-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 440.59pt, "ization [1]-[2]. These limitations have motivated the pur-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 452.11pt, "suit of alternative power conversion approaches that can ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 463.63pt, "achieve efficient voltage transformation within smaller ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 475.03pt, "footprints [3]-[4]. Piezoelectric transformers have emerged ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 486.55pt, "as a compelling candidate, as their ability to maintain high ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 498.07pt, "efficiency and power density in compact geometries makes ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 509.59pt, "them an attractive platform for next-generation compact ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 521.11pt, "power conversion systems [5]-[7]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 532.51pt, "Among various piezoelectric transformer configura-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 544.03pt, "tions, Rosen-type transformers have been extensively stud-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 555.55pt, "ied for their ability to achieve large voltage step-up ratios ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 567.07pt, "and high passive voltage gain in compact architectures [8]-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 578.62pt, "[9]. Early implementations using lead zirconate titanate ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 590.14pt, "(PZT) were widely adopted in power supplies and LCD ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 601.54pt, "backlighting systems [10]-[12]. The performance of PZT-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 613.06pt, "based Rosen transformers, though effective at moderate ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 624.58pt, "power levels, was ultimately constrained by intrinsic mate-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 636.1pt, "rial drawbacks, including high dielectric loss and thermal ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 647.62pt, "instability under large drive conditions, which degraded ef-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 659.14pt, "ficiency and long-term reliability [13]-[15]. As display ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 670.54pt, "technology transitioned to low-voltage LED lighting, the ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 682.06pt, "demand for high-voltage AC conversion decreased, result-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 693.58pt, "ing in a decline in research activity. More recently, piezoe-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 705.1pt, "lectric transformers have regained attention as a promising ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 716.62pt, "solution for compact, high-efficiency, magnetic-less power ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 728.14pt, "conversion, driven by the growing need for integrated high-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 739.56pt, "voltage amplification in modern electronics[16]-[17]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 751.08pt, "With advancements in piezoelectric materials, trans-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 762.6pt, "formers using aluminum nitride (AlN) [18]-[19] and quartz ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 134.66pt, "[20]-[21] have demonstrated the capability of efficient op-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 146.18pt, "eration at elevated frequencies. However, each material ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 157.7pt, "system presents intrinsic trade-offs that limit voltage am-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 169.1pt, "plification and energy transfer efficiency. AlN exhibits rel-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 180.62pt, "atively low electromechanical coupling (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.74pt, 180.62pt, "k²")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(475.06pt, 180.62pt, "), which restricts ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 192.14pt, "voltage gain and power throughput, while quartz achieves ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 203.66pt, "extremely high mechanical quality factors (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(491.16pt, 203.66pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.36pt, 203.66pt, ") but pos-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 215.18pt, "sesses extremely low coupling.  ")
  #line-at(324.43pt, 226.7pt, "Lithium niobate (LN) has recently emerged as a prom-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 238.1pt, "ising platform for high-performance transformers due to its ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 249.65pt, "combination of strong coupling, low acoustic loss, and ex-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 261.17pt, "cellent thermal stability. LN transformers demonstrated ef-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 272.69pt, "ficient power transfer and high voltage step-up in both lon-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 284.21pt, "gitudinal-extensional (LE) and thickness-extensional (TE) ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 295.61pt, "configurations, establishing LN’s potential for compact, ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 307.13pt, "high-frequency power conversion [22-24]. More recently, ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 318.65pt, "radial-mode LN transformers have demonstrated that in-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 330.17pt, "plane vibration with a central nodal region can minimize ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 341.69pt, "anchor loss, decouple impedance from resonance fre-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 353.21pt, "quency, and support scalable device geometries [25].  ")
  #line-at(324.43pt, 364.61pt, "Building on these insights, this work presents a two-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 376.13pt, "port radial-mode Rosen transformer on 36° Y-cut LN, ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 387.65pt, "achieving")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(345.31pt, 387.65pt, " k² ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(356.83pt, 387.65pt, "= 16.8%, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(394.78pt, 387.65pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(401.98pt, 387.65pt, " = 2500, and a figure of merit (FoM ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 399.17pt, "= ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.71pt, 399.17pt, "Q × k²")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(341.35pt, 399.17pt, ") of 420. The transformer delivers an open-circuit ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 410.71pt, "voltage gain of 45.6 V/V, demonstrating the strong poten-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 422.23pt, "tial of radial-mode LN structure for compact, high-effi-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 433.63pt, "ciency, magnetic-less piezoelectric power transformers. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.43pt, 458.47pt, "DESIGN AND SIMULATION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(324.43pt, 470.47pt, "The design of the two-port LN radial-mode Rosen ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 481.99pt, "transformer is illustrated in Fig. 1. The device employs a 1 ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 493.51pt, "mm thick, 36° Y-cut LN wafer with top and bottom elec-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 505.03pt, "trodes arranged in concentric geometries, as shown in Fig. ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 516.43pt, "1(a). The top view in Fig. 1(b) highlights the inner elec-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 527.95pt, "trode (VIN₁) and the outer ring electrode (VIN₂), while the ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 539.47pt, "bottom ground (GND) electrode is shown in Fig. 1(c). This ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 550.99pt, "electrode configuration creates a large capacitance contrast ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 562.51pt, "between port 1 (VIN")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(391.42pt, 563.47pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(394.66pt, 562.51pt, " and GND, thickness electrical field ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 573.94pt, "excitation via e")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(367.63pt, 574.9pt, "33")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(374.11pt, 573.94pt, ") and port 2 (VIN")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(444.34pt, 574.9pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(447.58pt, 573.94pt, " and GND, lateral elec-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 585.46pt, "trical field excitation via e")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(409.66pt, 586.42pt, "31 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(417.58pt, 585.46pt, "and e")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(438.46pt, 586.42pt, "32")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(444.94pt, 585.46pt, "), similar to longitudinal ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 596.98pt, "Rosen transformers [23], which establishes a strong imped-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 608.5pt, "ance ratio that enables substantial passive voltage gain, ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 620.02pt, "analogous to the turns-ratio effect in magnetic transform-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 631.54pt, "ers. The LN thickness and electrode geometry are carefully ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 642.94pt, "optimized to balance large impedance contrast while main-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 654.46pt, "taining strong electromechanical coupling across the radial ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 665.98pt, "mode for both ports. ")
  #line-at(324.43pt, 677.5pt, "To determine the optimal cut and coupling orientation, ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 689.02pt, "Fig. 2 plots the calculated piezoelectric coefficients and ef-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 700.54pt, "fective in-plane coupling factors as a function of in-plane ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 711.94pt, "rotation of 36-Y LN. Although certain LN wafer cuts ex-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 723.46pt, "hibit slightly higher piezoelectric coefficients, the 36° Y-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 735.1pt, "cut is selected as it can provide simultaneously high ")
