#original-page(594.72pt, 841.68pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 484.5pt), 55.5pt, 54pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(54.024pt, 385.01pt, "and 2(b) show the related piezoelectric coefficients, to-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 396.53pt, "gether with their associated coupling coefficients, enable ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 408.07pt, "efficient radial-mode operation for both ports.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 419.59pt, "To validate the proposed design, finite element analy-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 431.11pt, "sis (FEA) was performed using COMSOL Multiphysics to ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 442.51pt, "simulate both the admittance spectra and the displacement ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 454.03pt, "field. Figure 3(a) shows the simulated and fitted admittance ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 465.55pt, "responses of the two-port transformer. Figs. 3(b) and 3(c) ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 477.07pt, "show two resonances observed near 313 kHz and 345 kHz, ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 488.59pt, "corresponding to the fundamental radial mode and a spuri-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 499.99pt, "ous higher-order wine-glass overtone, respectively, con-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 511.51pt, "firming effective mode excitation. As shown in Fig. 3(d), ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 523.03pt, "the radial mode exhibits concentric, axisymmetric expan-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 534.55pt, "sion and contraction, with a zero-displacement node at the ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 546.07pt, "center of the disk, where the mounting is applied, and a ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 557.59pt, "maximum displacement near the outer edge. The corre-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 568.99pt, "sponding lateral stress distribution in Fig. 3(e) further cor-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 580.54pt, "roborates this behavior. The dominant stress component is ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 592.06pt, "confined to the active electrode region, with stress mini-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 603.58pt, "mum located at the center of the disk. Still, the stress near ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 615.1pt, "the disk edge will be used for port 2 excitation.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 626.62pt, "To quantitatively model this behavior, an equivalent-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 638.02pt, "circuit representation of the two-port radial-mode trans-")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 649.54pt, "former is developed in Fig. 4, including both the main tone ")
  #line-at(54.024pt, 661.06pt, "and the spurious mode. Each port is represented by a static ")
