  #line-at(306.43pt, 479.47pt, "This model, therefore, provides a compact yet physically ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 490.99pt, "meaningful framework for correlating simulated and meas-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 502.51pt, "ured data, guiding the subsequent device fabrication and ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 514.03pt, "experimental validation. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.43pt, 538.87pt, "FABRICATION AND MEASUREMENT")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324.43pt, 550.75pt, "The transformer was fabricated using standard micro-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 562.27pt, "fabrication processes. The top electrodes (VIN₁ and VIN₂) ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 573.82pt, "were first defined through standard photolithography, fol-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 585.34pt, "lowed by electron-beam metal deposition and lift-off to ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 596.86pt, "form the concentric input and output electrodes. A titanium ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 608.38pt, "(Ti) adhesion layer was deposited prior to the copper (Cu) ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 619.78pt, "layer to improve adhesion to the LN substrate. The total ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 631.3pt, "metal thickness was approximately 400 nm (Ti/Cu). The ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 642.82pt, "backside ground electrode (GND) was subsequently pat-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 654.34pt, "terned using backside alignment to mirror the top VIN₁ re-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 665.86pt, "gion, ensuring proper field symmetry and uniform electric ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 677.26pt, "excitation across the LN thickness. Cu was chosen as the ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 688.78pt, "electrode material due to its high electrical conductivity, ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 700.3pt, "power-handling capability, and compatibility with subse-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 711.82pt, "quent wire-bonding and packaging processes.  After metal-")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 723.34pt, "lization, the wafer was diced into individual dies as shown ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 734.86pt, "in Fig. 5(a).  ")
  #line-at(324.43pt, 746.28pt, "For electrical characterization, the diced LN dies were ")
  #line-at(306.43pt, 757.8pt, "mounted and wire-bonded onto a custom-designed PCB ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
